# 2. Restriction on Competing Services

## 2.1. Separate Authorization Required

Notwithstanding any other provision of this License, a Licensee must not use the Covered Work, or any modified or derivative version thereof, to develop, operate, distribute, sublicense, or commercially provide a Competing Service without a separate Commercial Agreement expressly authorizing such activity.

## 2.2. Scope of Restriction

This restriction applies regardless of whether the Verification Targets used by the Competing Service consist of Public Source Code or Private Source Code.

Permission to perform free Verification of Public Source Code does not grant permission to commercially offer Axiom's core verification functionality as a competing product or service.

## 2.3. Examples of Competing Services

A Competing Service includes, without limitation:

1. A paid hosted Verification service built upon Axiom.
2. A commercial Verification platform that embeds Axiom as its underlying Verification engine.
3. A commercial product or service that exposes Axiom's core Verification functionality to third parties.
4. A commercial offering that redistributes, sublicenses, or embeds Axiom or a derivative version thereof as a substitute for Axiom's core Verification service.

Whether an offering constitutes a Competing Service shall be determined by its actual functionality, commercial purpose, service structure, and substantive relationship to Axiom's core Verification functionality.

## 2.4. Internal Commercial Use Is Not Prohibited

An organization may use Axiom internally for its own software development, testing, Verification, and production activities.

Such internal use does not, by itself, constitute a Competing Service.

However, Verification of Private Source Code remains subject to Section 1.2.

## 2.5. Ordinary Development and Consulting Services

Ordinary software development, consulting, research, education, or professional services in which Axiom is merely an incidental tool do not, by themselves, constitute a Competing Service.

However, this exception does not apply where Axiom's core Verification functionality is independently offered to third parties as a commercial Verification product or service.

## 2.6. Separate Commercial Agreements

The Licensor may grant separate commercial rights for hosted services, OEM distribution, embedding, resale, enterprise deployment, service-provider distribution, or other commercial arrangements through a Commercial Agreement.

