# 3. Definitions

For purposes of this License, the following terms shall have the meanings set forth below.

## 3.1. Licensor

"Licensor" means Suhyok Yoon, as the initial licensor and initial rights holder of the rights in the Covered Work that Suhyok Yoon owns or is legally authorized to license.

"Licensor" also includes any lawful successor or assignee that acquires the rights necessary to administer this License and license the relevant portions of the Covered Work.

## 3.2. Licensee

"Licensee" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights granted under this License.

## 3.3. Covered Work

"Covered Work" means the Axiom software project and its associated source code, object code, documentation, configuration files, build scripts, and other materials distributed under this License.

Covered Work includes all Historical Versions falling within the scope of Section 4.

Third-Party Materials that are not owned or controlled by the Licensor are excluded from the Covered Work to the extent of the relevant third-party rights.

## 3.4. Source Code

"Source Code" means the preferred form of the Covered Work for making modifications, including source files, build scripts, interface definitions, and other materials necessary to understand and modify the Covered Work.

## 3.5. Public Source Code

"Public Source Code" means source code made available for inspection by the general public without individual access approval or confidentiality obligations.

Source code available through a publicly accessible repository or equivalent public distribution mechanism qualifies as Public Source Code, even if ordinary registration or account creation is required, provided that any member of the general public may obtain access through generally available procedures.

The following do not qualify as Public Source Code:

1. Source code accessible only to invited or individually approved users.
2. Private repositories, branches, pull requests, or code review materials.
3. Source code accessible under a non-disclosure agreement or other confidentiality obligation.
4. Source code subject to access restrictions that prevent the general public from inspecting it.

## 3.6. Private Source Code

"Private Source Code" means all source code that does not satisfy the definition of Public Source Code.

Public Source Code and Private Source Code are mutually exclusive and collectively exhaustive categories.

## 3.7. Verification

"Verification" means any exercise of the analysis, proof, validation, verification, or certification functionality of the Covered Work to evaluate, analyze, prove, validate, or otherwise establish properties, correctness claims, or other propositions concerning a Verification Target.

Verification includes such exercise regardless of the interface or mechanism through which that functionality is invoked, including command-line tools, MCP or other protocol servers, programming APIs, direct library calls, embedded or hosted deployments, or direct use of the underlying verification engine.

The following do not, by themselves, constitute Verification:

1. File management, output format conversion, report rendering, or other ancillary functions that do not invoke the verification functionality of the Covered Work.
2. Reuse of general-purpose utilities of the Covered Work (such as hashing, serialization, or command-line plumbing) in works unrelated to the verification functionality of the Covered Work.
3. Building, packaging, distributing, or hosting the Covered Work without exercising its verification functionality on any Verification Target.

## 3.8. Verification Target

"Verification Target" means the source code, program, repository, project, or expressly designated portion thereof that is subject to a particular Verification execution.

## 3.9. Verification Scope

"Verification Scope" means the complete scope of source code, dependencies, and related materials that Axiom actually reads, loads, analyzes, or includes in a particular Verification execution or its proof obligations.

## 3.10. Mixed Verification

"Mixed Verification" means a Verification execution in which Public Source Code and Private Source Code are jointly included in the same Verification Scope.

## 3.11. Competing Service

"Competing Service" means a product or service whose primary or material commercial function is to provide third parties with automated software Verification capabilities that materially substitute for the core Verification functionality of Axiom, where such capabilities are implemented using the Covered Work or a modified or derivative version thereof.

## 3.12. Non-Commercial Personal Use

"Non-Commercial Personal Use" means use by an individual solely for personal hobby, learning, research, or experimentation, without providing Verification as a paid or otherwise commercially compensated service.

Use by or on behalf of a company, organization, or other legal entity does not qualify as Non-Commercial Personal Use.

## 3.13. Commercial Agreement

"Commercial Agreement" means a separate written agreement or commercial license issued by the Licensor or an authorized successor or assignee, granting additional rights or permissions that are not available under this License without separate authorization or payment.

## 3.14. Third-Party Materials

"Third-Party Materials" means software, libraries, code, documentation, or other materials that are not owned or controlled by the Licensor and are distributed under their own applicable licenses or terms.

## 3.15. Official Axiom Repository

"Official Axiom Repository" means the official Git repository designated by the Licensor as the source repository for the Axiom project.

If the Licensor moves or changes the official source repository, the lawfully designated successor repository shall also qualify as the Official Axiom Repository.

## 3.16. Historical Version

"Historical Version" means any previous version, revision, commit, or snapshot of the Covered Work preserved in the Git history of the Official Axiom Repository.

## 3.17. Initial Publication

"Initial Publication" means the first public distribution of this License by the Licensor together with the Axiom project.

