# 10. License Duration and Termination

## 10.1. Duration

This License is perpetual unless terminated in accordance with this Section.

There is no automatic expiration date or automatic conversion to an open-source license.

## 10.2. Termination for Material Breach

If the Licensee materially violates this License, the Licensor may provide written notice identifying the violation and the steps required to remedy it.

Where the violation is capable of remedy, the Licensee shall have thirty (30) days from receipt of such notice to cure the violation.

If the violation is not cured within that period, the rights granted to the Licensee under this License shall terminate automatically.

This cure period does not apply to violations for which immediate termination is permitted by applicable law.

## 10.3. Reinstatement

If the rights granted under this License terminate, the Licensee must cease all use of the Covered Work that is no longer authorized.

Where the violation has been remedied, the Licensee may request reinstatement from the Licensor or an authorized successor or assignee.

Reinstatement requires written confirmation from the Licensor or such authorized successor or assignee.

## 10.4. Effect of Termination and Accrued Rights

Termination does not automatically invalidate permissions or licenses separately granted under a valid Commercial Agreement, except as provided in that agreement.

Termination or a subsequent licensing change does not retroactively revoke rights properly exercised or permissions validly granted before termination.

However, where termination results from the Licensee's own breach, any rights that may lawfully be revoked under applicable law may be revoked.

